  "raw_label": "1",
  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Nagappan vs Food Inspector on 6 June, 2018 Author: G.R.Swaminathan Bench: G.R.Swaminathan Before The Madurai Bench Of Madras High Court Dated: 06.06.2018 Coram The Honourable Mr.Justice G.R.Swaminathan Crl OP(MD)No.5638 of 2012 and MP(MD)No.2 of 2012 1.Nagappan 2.R.K.Venkatraman 3.R.K.Sivakumar 4.R.K.Suresh 5.R.K.Lakshmi 6.Hotel Dakshin High Power V Hotel Private Ltd., No.43, 44, Kuruvikaran Road, Madurai. ... Petitioners Vs. Food Inspector, Madurai Corporation, Madurai. ... Respondent Prayer : Criminal Original Petition is filed under Section 482 of the Criminal Procedure Code to call for the records pertaining to the proceedings in C.C.No.54 of 2010 pending on the file of the Judicial Magistrate No.I, Madurai and quash the same as against the petitioners are concerned and quash the same. For Petitioner : Mr.A.Uthayakumar Nagappan vs Food Inspector on 6 June, 2018 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/5638492/ 1 For Respondents : Mr.A.Robinson, Government Advocate :Order",
    "facts": "The petitioners are figuring as accused in CC.No.54 of 2010 on the file of the learned Judicial Magistrate No.I, Madurai for the offences under Sections 16(1)(a)(i) and (ii) r/w 7(i)(v) and (a) and (m) of Prevention of Food Adulteration Act, 1954 and Rule 50(1) of Prevention of Food Adulteration Rules, 1955 and 7(i) 16(1)(a) (1) r/w Section 2(1a) (a) (i) and 2(ix) (k) of Prevention of Food Adulteration Act. 2.In this case, food sample was seized on 04.06.2009. The report of the Public Analyst was received on 06.7.2009. But, notice was served on the petitioners only on 02.03.2010. Thus, there has been a lapse of a clear eight months in the process. Therefore, the petitioners have been deprived of the valuable right of re-analysis. In similar circumstance, the prosecution was [LEAKAGE_MASK] by this Court in the decision reported in (2011) 3 MLJ (Crl) 99 (T.R.S.Vijayaraj v. Commissioner).",
    "arguments": "",
    "petitioner_arguments": "",
    "respondent_arguments": "",
    "other_lawyer_arguments": ""
  },
